window.docContents[243].resolve({"/Environment/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Environment--___":{"contents":"This API abstracts away the term manager completely and enforces manager-consistency statically\nusing a type-class called Ω. Virtually all types in this library have an implicit Ω\nargument that can be thought of as representing a specific term manager. On the sort type for\ninstance:\n\n#check Srt\n\n\nCvc.Srt [Ω] : Type\n\n\nΩ is an empty Prop type-class and will be erased at runtime; note that you cannot\nbuild an instance yourself as the constructor is private.\n\nArgument of the Env monad representing a specific term manager.\n\nΩ is tied to cvc.lean's environment monad Env: Env α, or more precisely\n@Env inst α where (inst : Ω), corresponds to code that uses a specific term manager\nto produce a value of type α.\nCvc5's term manager handles term/sort perfect sharingAlso known as hash-consing:\nbuilding the same term twice produces the same (reference to the same) term, meaning physical\n(reference) equality is structural equality..\n\nThe first problem Ω and Env solve is that manipulating a value v tied to manager\nm after m has been freed is unsafe as freeing m frees v, so v should only live as long as\nm is alive. So most features in this library produce an Env _ output.\n\nSecond, as mentioned above, values tied to different managers should never interact as that would\ncause a runtime error. By encoding a specific term manager through an Ω-value, cvc.lean can\ntype-check that sorts/terms/solvers/etc. are compatible by making sure they agree on their\nΩ-value.\n\nFor example, the function building an array-sort makes sure the index and element sorts agree on\ntheir manager, and keeps track of the manager associated to the resulting sort by having all of\nthem agree on their Ω.\n\nCreates the sort of arrays from idx to elm, e.g. idx.arrayTo elm.\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level CVC5 API\u0009Environment","header":"2.1. Ω","id":"/Environment/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Environment--___"}});